---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Okhla | Nagrik Party"
  description="Okhla Assembly Constituency: the anchor constituency and first public proof point of Nagrik Party's civic work approach."
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="mini-label" style="background: rgba(179, 74, 21, 0.08); color: var(--saffron);">
        ANCHOR CONSTITUENCY · SOUTH-EAST DELHI
      </div>
      <h1 style="font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4vw, 3rem); font-family: var(--font-serif); margin: 10px 0 14px;">
        Okhla Assembly Constituency
      </h1>
      <p class="page-copy">
        Okhla Assembly Constituency is where Founder Arsalan Azad contested as an independent candidate in 2025. It serves as the initial proof point of the party's civic accountability model across local wards.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="split">
        <div class="legal-article">
          <h2>Why Okhla Matters</h2>
          <p>
            Okhla is where Arsalan Azad first engaged in direct electoral politics. The constituency represents the practical transition from an independent campaign to durable political infrastructure. The local issues documented during the 2025 campaign, including civic infrastructure, women safety, sanitation, and public utilities, form the basis of Nagrik Party's issue-first approach.
          </p>

          <h2>Anchor Constituency Model</h2>
          <p>
            Okhla is the first constituency where Nagrik Party demonstrates its full civic operations model: issue intake from residents, volunteer-led verification, lawful complaint filing, public status tracking, and area-wise manifesto building. The model developed here will be extended across Delhi's other 69 Assembly constituencies.
          </p>

          <h2>Local Issues Pipeline</h2>
          <p>
            Citizens in Okhla can report civic issues directly through this platform. Reported issues go through verification, classification, and lawful escalation. Unresolved issues become part of the area manifesto, a living document that reflects what residents actually need.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <div style="display: grid; gap: 14px;">
            <div class="card feature" style="padding: 18px;">
              <span class="mini-label">Location</span>
              <h3 style="font-size: 20px; margin-top: 8px;">South-East Delhi</h3>
            </div>
            <div class="card feature" style="padding: 18px;">
              <span class="mini-label">Status</span>
              <h3 style="font-size: 20px; margin-top: 8px;">Anchor Constituency</h3>
              <p style="font-size: 14px;">First constituency for the full civic operations model.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card feature" style="padding: 18px;">
              <span class="mini-label">Get Involved</span>
              <div style="display: grid; gap: 10px; margin-top: 10px;">
                <a class="button green" href="/issues" style="justify-content: start;">
                  Report an Okhla Issue
                </a>
                <a class="button" href="/volunteer" style="justify-content: start;">
                  Volunteer in Okhla
                </a>
                <a class="button" href="/membership" style="justify-content: start;">
                  Apply for Membership
                </a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band-soft">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="action-row" style="justify-content: center;">
        <a class="button" href="/founder">
          &larr; Back to Founder
        </a>
        <a class="button" href="/president/delhi-2025">
          &larr; Delhi 2025
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
